    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bracketed\n\n### Description\n\nIt seems that **mini.bracketed** (and other components) already cover most of [unimpaired's](https://github.com/tpope/vim-unimpaired) functionality.\nHowever, I think the quick toggles are still missing and might be a nice addition.\nHere the corresponding section from unimpaired's help file.\n\n```\nOPTION TOGGLING                                 *unimpaired-toggling*\n\nOn\tOff\tToggle\tOption\n*[ob*\t*]ob*\t*yob*\t'background' (dark is off, light is on)\n*[oc*\t*]oc*\t*yoc*\t'cursorline'\n*[od*\t*]od*\t*yod*\t'diff' (actually |:diffthis| / |:diffoff|)\n*[oh*\t*]oh*\t*yoh*\t'hlsearch'\n*[oi*\t*]oi*\t*yoi*\t'ignorecase'\n*[ol*\t*]ol*\t*yol*\t'list'\n*[on*\t*]on*\t*yon*\t'number'\n*[or*\t*]or*\t*yor*\t'relativenumber'\n*[os*\t*]os*\t*yos*\t'spell'\n*[ot*\t*]ot*\t*yot*\t'colorcolumn' (\"+1\" or last used value)\n*[ou*\t*]ou*\t*you*\t'cursorcolumn'\n*[ov*\t*]ov*\t*yov*\t'virtualedit'\n*[ow*\t*]ow*\t*yow*\t'wrap'\n*[ox*\t*]ox*\t*yox*\t'cursorline' 'cursorcolumn' (x as in crosshairs)\n\nThe mnemonic for y is that if you tilt it a bit it looks like a switch.\n\n                                                *<s* *>s* *=s*\nAlternative prefixes for on/off/toggle: <s, >s, =s.\n```\n\nI've even extended this with making `yof` toggle auto-word wrapping\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"n\", \"yof\", function()\n\tif vim.opt_local.formatoptions:get().a then\n\t\tvim.opt_local.formatoptions:remove(\"a\")\n\t\tprint(\"Auto wordwrap disabled\")\n\telse\n\t\tvim.opt_local.formatoptions:append(\"a\")\n\t\tprint(\"Auto wordwrap enabled\")\n\tend\nend, { desc = \"Toggle auto wordwrap\" })\n```\n\nNote: I added this to the **mini.bracketed** section, but this could easily go into another module or even become its own.",
