        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThis indeed is already a part of another module, ['mini.basics'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/44a3ab2bc6b40edeb7a76359826c9779d5c70cb5/doc/mini-basics.txt#L251), as it felt a little out of place being part of 'mini.bracketed' directly. By default it uses `\\` prefix instead of `yo` from 'vim-unimpaired', as it requires less keys pressed, has better (at list in my opinion) mnemonic, and doesn't start with built-in operator (which gets confusing very quickly). The prefix can be customized via [`config.mapping.option_toggle_prefix`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/44a3ab2bc6b40edeb7a76359826c9779d5c70cb5/doc/mini-basics.txt#L99).\n\nClosing as already implemented in another module.",
